<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.11.1: Relating a Quadratic Function and Its Zeros</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02272</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.11.1: Relating a Quadratic Function and Its Zeros</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bd6b7da9-34fa-4e45-87b3-555b9d2b5417</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Write the quadratic function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in factored form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Enter the quadratic function in factored form.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00004"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">What are the solutions of the quadratic equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Enter the solutions of the quadratic equation.</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00018">Graph the quadratic function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course.</para>
          <media alt="...">
            <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
          </media>
          <para id="para-00010">What are the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Enter the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00013"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or 4 and 5</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00014">Marcus states that the zeros of the function of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> are 4 and 5. Do you agree? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Enter your answer and your reasoning.</para>
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00017">Yes, 4 and 5 are the input values that result in an output of 0. When the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is graphed, it crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>